      "note": "Provisional machine alignment by Codex, independent Tibetan-first proposal. brgya pa is the attested abbreviated work title 400 Verses, not a numerical claim that brgya means four hundred; corpus examples of the full bzhi brgya pa title support the title convention. yang dag don is the recurring philosophical expression reality, not a separately banked don-to-reality claim. The commentary's positive rtog pa yod pa kho nas yod pa nyid dang clause is omitted as compressed into the negative English formulation; rtog pa med par is a unique whole phrase to prevent attaching its conceptions to the earlier omitted rtog pa. Existence negatives are complete phrases; no unsupported not-inside-cannot subword is used. thag pa bsdogs pa is a compositional phrase coil of rope, supported also by EM:264's coiled rope, not a d5 compound. The closing de la bltos te dependence construction is unresolved against through the process of conceptualization and is omitted rather than nulled; the clear final rtog pa and skye ba retain Conception and occur. Supplied participants and auxiliaries remain unwrapped. C16:808 shares the Tibetan fields but changes English vocabulary; P7:9 has a shorter English continuation, and ILL:1109 does not translate the closing definitions. Those witnesses do not prove the disputed continuation or any independent ingestion history."
